# Front Matter

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:mdex, "~> 0.14"},
  {:yaml_elixir, "~> 2.12"}
])
```

## Intro

Set the `front_matter_delimiter` extension option to parse front matter into an `MDEx.FrontMatter` node. Its `literal` holds the raw text, delimiters included, so remove the delimiters and decode the rest with a library for its format, YAML in this example.

## Example

```elixir
markdown = """
---
title: Orders
description: One row per completed customer order.
tags: [sales, revenue]
---

# Orders
"""

document = MDEx.parse_document!(markdown, extension: [front_matter_delimiter: "---"])

[%MDEx.FrontMatter{literal: literal}] = document[MDEx.FrontMatter]

literal
|> String.trim()
|> String.trim_leading("---")
|> String.trim_trailing("---")
|> YamlElixir.read_from_string!()
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%{
  "description" => "One row per completed customer order.",
  "tags" => ["sales", "revenue"],
  "title" => "Orders"
}
```
